# Template discovery, money splash, idle board (s3.1.7)

Resume: `@templates$` / `$money-rain$`.

## Venue-exclusive templates

- Patron picker reads only packaged `window.SHOUTOUT_TEMPLATES` (never the Firestore `templates` collection). Ids = `blackwhite` + `location.templates` + templates whose `venueIds` include the venue + standard ids, then `status==='active'` + `templateFitsVenue`.
- Default view: Default Template card, then **Exclusive at {venue}** (`template.venueExclusive`, all 11 chrome packs) listing every record whose `venueIds` includes the current venue.
- Search box (`submitCategoryVenueQuery`) and FloqAi intents (`action:"template"`) route template names through `exclusiveTemplateForQuery` (name + `searchAliases`, accent/punctuation-insensitive, ≥ 4 chars) → `startTemplateShoutout`: one venue → ad splash → composer; several → venue grid filtered to `venueIds`; the name is pre-filled into `#templateSearch`.
- Football Intro (formerly Zebbies All-Stars): `zebbies-garden-washington-dc`, `heist-washington-dc`, `temp-democlub-1` (Aurelia). Backend checkout set must match. 96×48 only since s3.1.11 — see `design-notes-football-intro-venues.mdc`.

## Template Preview (s3.1.11)

- `floqr-template-preview.js` → `window.FLOQRTemplatePreview` (`sampleFor`, `formatsFor`, `previewUrl`, `open`). Patron picker `templateCard` adds **Preview** (`data-template-preview`) on every official card (default, Exclusive, search results). Soccer photo-team cards resolve through `FLOQRSoccerPhotoTeams()`.
- Modal iframe = `display.html?location=…&template=…&main=…&screen=<fmt>&preview=1` (URL-preview mode paints from the URL and never reads Firestore). **No `?v=`** on this Display URL. Size buttons = `overlappingFormatIds(template, venue)` ∩ supported layouts, largest first.
- Sample by `FLOQRTextLayout.profileId`: `splitMedia` → `images/template-preview/sample-birthday.jpg` (birthday) / `sample-romance.jpg` (anniversary, engagement, fiancé); `christine` → `sample-club-night.jpg`; `footballIntro` → four `football-player-{1..4}.svg` + `{BRAND} FOOTBALL INTRO`; `nameOnly` → `@FloqrStar`; `classicBoard` → uppercase, no emoji; `car` → RIDIN' RARI; jerseys → NYX + number with the team photo back; others → HAPPY BIRTHDAY MAYA! 🎉. Photos are AI-generated still lifes (no people), 640 px JPEG.
- Strings `templatePreview.*` (11 chrome packs); help `help-template-preview` (patron).

## Venue template tags + template roles (s3.1.11)

- Owner ask: venue/club admins **or their assigned operatives** add tags to every template offered at their venue. Roles: **Administer Templates** → Template Administrator (read, write, delete); **Manage Templates** → Template Manager (read, write).
- Data: `venueTemplateTags/{locationId}__{templateId}` `{clubLocationId, templateId, tags[] ≤30, updatedByUid, updatedByEmail, updatedAt, revision}`; `venueTemplateRoles/{locationId}_{uid}` `{clubLocationId, uid, email, displayName, role: administrator|manager, status: active|revoked, grantedByUid, grantedByEmail, updatedAt}`.
- Rules (control, not the UI): tags public read (patron search). Create = `canManageTemplates`. Update = administrator, **or** manager only when `tags.hasAll(oldTags)` (a manager can add, never remove). Delete = administrator. Club managers (`isClubManager`) are always administrators. Role docs: only `isClubManager(clubId)` can write; `get` by the holder or a club manager (no list queries — read by doc id).
- Why not `clubEmployeeDesignations.rolePermissions`: that collection is writable by any signed-in user (open finding), so it is only the **editor**. Club Admin → REP ticks `administerTemplates` / `manageTemplates`; `admin-rep-extension.js` `syncTemplateRoles` writes the role doc (Administer wins) and sends an Inbox row `type:"templateRole"` → `./template-tags.html?location=…&v=<APP_V>` (label “Open template tags”). Unticking writes `status:"revoked"`.
- Page `template-tags.html` (satellite, `FLOQRSessionShell`) lists `FLOQRTemplateTags.templatesForVenue` (same set as the patron picker), shows FLOQR tags read-only and venue tags as chips (× only for administrators). Club Admin card “Manage template tags” links there.
- Search: patron `templateSearchText` and card tag chips include venue tags (`ensureVenueTemplateTags` per venue); Club Admin repository search too. Help `help-template-tags` (venueAdmin + serviceMember).

## Club Admin template repository + forgiving match (s3.1.8)

- Heist was already assigned every Heist template (live `clubLocations/heist-washington-dc.templates` + packaged `templates` + `venueIds`; checkout `HEIST_ART_TEMPLATE_IDS`). The s3.1.8 bug was **findability**, not assignment.
- `window.FLOQRTemplateMatch` (`shared-data.js`): `normalize` (NFD, accent strip, lowercase), `phraseMatches(query, phrase)` (every phrase word must match, or the first two of a 3+ word name since s3.1.10; plural `s` stems; **one** typo allowed only when the phrase has ≥ 2 words of ≥ 4 chars, so "looked up" never routes to "Locked Up"), `textMatches(query, text)` (admin filter: each query word is a substring or within edit distance 1, 2 for ≥ 7 chars), `templateText(template)`.
- Used by patron `exclusiveTemplateForQuery`, Club Admin `templateMatchesQuery`. FloqAi tengo intent regex accepts `te\w{2,3} mucho(s) d[oó]lar`.
- `renderClubTemplateBackgrounds` dedupes by `template.id` (alias `heistRedLux` shares `id:"heistVaultDollars"`), orders club-exclusive (`venueIds` includes the club) → assigned → rest, and tags exclusives with **Exclusive at {venue}**.
- Seed script `functions/scripts/onboard-dc-venues.js` assigns `heistVaultDollars` (not the alias).
- Admin help id `help-club-template-repository` (venueAdmin, all 11 langs).

## Tengo muchos dólares (`heistVaultDollars`, legacy `heistRedLux`)

Template fields (s3.1.12): `moneyRain:true`, `moneyRainDelaySeconds:5`, `moneySplashSeconds:10` (documentary), `messageDurationSeconds:15` (= words + splash), `brandSlideSeconds:8`. `display-app.js` `syncMoneyRain` builds `#displayMoneyRain` right after `#displayBackground` (z-index 1). `MONEY_RAIN_DELAY_SECONDS = 40` is only the fallback for templates without the field.

Every Heist message phase (`scheduleHeistMessageThenBrandSlide`) calls `replayMoneyRain(template)`, so the timeline restarts from 0 on the first run **and** after every brand slide:

| Time from message-phase start | Layer classes | What shows |
|---|---|---|
| 0 → 5 s | none | Name + typed line over the vault (typing finishes ≤ 5 s: `TYPED_LINE_START_MS 500` + 100 ms/glyph) |
| 5 s | `is-blast` (2.6 s) + canvas `money-shake` (0.7 s, background only) | Flash, shockwave ring, steel door disc blows toward the viewer, shards, smoke |
| 5 s | `is-flood` (7.4 s) | 8×6 grid of 25vw bills bursts from the vault (48% / 43%) and covers the whole board, then falls away |
| 9.2 s → 15 s | `is-stream` | 30 smaller (15vw) bills keep splashing from the vault |
| 15 s → 23 s | brand slide | HEIST logo over WASHINGTON DC; money layer faded out; then loop |

- s3.1.11 and earlier keyed the blast to `approvedAt` + 40 s, which landed after the first 20 s brand slide — the owner saw no splash on the first run. `moneyRainStartMs` was removed; do not reintroduce an approvedAt-based offset.
- `purgeDisplaySurface` → `stopMoneyRain` clears timers. A re-render restarts the phase (same as the typed line).
- **Verbiage on top:** `.money-rain-active .display-text-overlay{z-index:5}` + heavy dark text-shadow on `#displayMain`, `#displaySub`, `.classic-board-lines b`. Never put bills above the text overlay.
- **Brand slide (s3.1.12, all Heist templates):** `display.html` / `display2.html` `#heistBrandLogo` + `#heistBrandName`. The logo spells HEIST, so no "HEIST DC" word; label = `loc.brandSlideLabel` (Heist: "Washington DC") else `HEIST_BRAND_SLIDE_LABEL` "WASHINGTON DC", uppercase. Logo stacked over label in a flex column, centered horizontally and vertically on the board (vw/vh sizing, works on 96×48 / 64×48 / 64×32). `primeHeistBrandSlide()` sets the logo `src` at message-phase start so the slide never opens on an unloaded image.
- **Typed board size (s3.1.12):** name `min(19.55vh, 138vw / glyphs)`, line `min(12.08vh, 6.44vw)` (+15% over s3.1.11), board `translateY(-6vh)`.
- **Bill art (s3.1.10):** `.money-bill-face` uses `images/heist/heist-novelty-100-trump.jpg` (800×450, 16:9 → bill height `--bw * .5625`). Owner asked for an official-looking $100 with Donald Trump in the portrait. It is a **novelty** prop: no real signatures, no Treasury seal, no serial numbers, no "legal tender" wording. Never regenerate with real officials' signatures or a Treasury-like seal.

### Name-only + typed line (s3.1.10)

- Template fields: `nameOnly:true`, `maxNameCharacters:14`, `typedLine:'Tengo muchos dólares... I just did a heist!'` (official spelling; the owner typed "Tendo mucho dolares"). `lineCount` / caps unchanged, so checkout `fitCheckoutDisplayText` keeps the ≤ 14-glyph name on one row (no backend change).
- Composer: `floqr-name-shoutout.js` → `window.FLOQRNameShoutout` (`isNameOnly`, `maxName`, `capName`, `suggestions`, `bind`). `patron-app.js` `syncNameShoutoutFields()` (called from `syncSoccerJerseyFields`) hides `#mainText`, attribution controls and the recommendations card, shows `#nameShoutoutFields`, writes the name into `#mainText` and clears `#subText`. Suggestions: own Mingl handle → own Instagram → own display name, then public profiles (`users` where `publicProfileVisibility === "public"`, ≤ 500, lazy on focus) Mingl + Instagram handles. Accent/`@`-folded substring on value or display name; starts-with first; dedupe; max 8. Free text is allowed (a name needn't be a FLOQR user).
- Board: `display-app.js` text-overlay branch → `typedLineBoardHtml(name, typedLine)` (big name, then a monospace gold line). `startTypedLine()` types one glyph every 100 ms after 500 ms (s3.1.12; was 110 / 900) with a blinking caret; re-runs every Heist message phase (after the brand slide). Idle CTA never uses the typed board. s3.1.11: line text “Tengo muchos dólares... I just did a heist!” and bigger type (`.typed-line` `font-size:min(10.5vh,5.6vw)`, `width:96%`, two rows on 96×48). `stopTypedLine()` on every render and in `purgeDisplaySurface`.

## Search box: partial names + events and clubs (s3.1.10)

- `phraseMatches` also accepts the **first two words** of a 3+ word name when both are ≥ 4 chars (still one typo max): "Tendo Mucho" → Tengo muchos dólares. "police car" does not route to "police car arrest" (second word < 4).
- `submitCategoryVenueQuery`: when `FLOQRVenueQuery.parse` finds no type in the query (`typeSource !== "query"`), listing type is `all` → `renderAllGrid` renders an **Events** section and a **Clubs & venues** section (`listing.searchAll`, `listing.sectionEvents`, `listing.sectionVenues`). Typing a type later in the listing box switches to that type. Ad splash still gets `events` for `all`.

## Idle board

- Display 1 idle text is always `Use ShoutOut @ {club}` (`clubDefaultMainText`; configured `defaultMain` is ignored on primary). Display 2 keeps the SupRstar idle CTA.
- Display treats any doc with `status:"default"`, `idleCta`, missing doc, or no status + no text/media as idle → `defaultClubDisplayPayload()`.
- `expireLiveShoutouts` (every minute) overwrites expired `liveContent` with `idleLiveContentAfterExpiry` (blackwhite, `Use ShoutOut @ {club}`, `idleCta:true`, `source:"automaticTenMinuteReset"`). No Heist exception. The helper is **not** exported (index.js spreads module exports into deployed functions).
- **Reset display to default** writes the same text + `idleCta:true`.
- **s3.1.9 bug + fix:** approve merges onto the idle doc, so `idleCta:true` / `source:automaticTenMinuteReset` survived and the board hid the approved ShoutOut (Heist SO-0752287). Board uses `isIdlePayload` (status `approved`/`live`/`preview` is never idle). Club Admin approve and `messagingInboundWebhook` approve write `idleCta:false`, a `source`, and delete `expiredAt`.

